The generated lists include IP prefixes taken from third-party sources
listed in tools/sources.json and overlay/sources.json.

RockBlack-VPN/ip-address
  https://github.com/RockBlack-VPN/ip-address
  MIT License, Copyright 2024
  Per-service Keenetic `route ADD` trees (`Global/`, `RU-RU/`).
  This repository collapses each tree into one list and writes
  `:: rem <folder>` on each line. Emits `global.bat` and `ru.bat`.

misakaio/chnroutes2
  https://github.com/misakaio/chnroutes2
  CC-BY-SA 2.0
  Mainland China IPv4 prefixes from BGP, updated hourly.
  Emits `cn.bat` as one service named China.
  Share-alike applies to the generated China prefixes.

farshidmousavii/iran-ip-ranges
  https://github.com/farshidmousavii/iran-ip-ranges
  MIT License
  Iran IPv4 prefixes announced in RIPE Stat, refreshed every 6 hours.
  Emits `ir.bat` as one service named Iran.

ipverse/as-ip-blocks
  https://github.com/ipverse/as-ip-blocks
  CC0 1.0 Universal
  BGP-announced IPv4 prefixes by ASN, updated daily.
  Feeds overlay services that have their own AS (Kaspi, Halyk, BCC,
  Jusan, Forte, NITEC/Egov, Priorbank, NCES, BeCloud).
  Emits into `kz.bat` and `by.bat`. Host prefixes on shared ISPs
  live as files under overlay/kz/ and overlay/by/.

Files under overlay/ are contributed in this repository and keep
the license of their authors unless a file says otherwise.

Upstream copyright notices are preserved here as required by MIT / CC-BY-SA.
The converter (tools/convert.py) is original work of a3app.
